 "marks": [
  {
   "d": "2021-12-06",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "In addition to a sizeable currency headwind, like most industrial companies, we are facing increased raw material and energy costs, which will impact us particularly in the first half, although mitigation plans are progressing.",
   "file": "20211206_VCT_Victrex-plc---Preliminary-Results-2021.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-02-11",
   "doc": "Q1 TU",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "Whilst we anticipate further volume improvement across several end markets, we are mindful of headwinds including currency, raw material costs and increasing energy inflation.",
   "file": "20220211_VCT_AGM-&-Q1-Interim-Management-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-05-09",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "Nevertheless, for FY 2022 as a whole, we remain focused on delivering good year-on-year growth.",
   "file": "20220509_VCT_Victrex-plc---Interim-Results-2022.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-07-07",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "Whilst we are mindful of uncertainty in the global economic outlook, we remain on track for delivering full year expectations.",
   "file": "20220707_VCT_Victrex-Q3-Interim-Management-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-12-06",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "Overall, we have seen a steady start to the year and are focused on modest revenue and profit growth.",
   "file": "20221206_VCT_Victrex-plc---Preliminary-Results-2022.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-02-10",
   "doc": "Q1 TU",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "However, the Group saw softer volumes during Q1 and the macro-economic environment remains uncertain, with ongoing weakness in several end-markets.",
   "file": "20230210_VCT_AGM-&-Q1-Interim-Management-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-05-09",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "Delivering a PBT performance in line with FY 2022 and current expectations assumes a step up in demand during the latter part of the second half, driven by macro-economic conditions.",
   "file": "20230509_VCT_Victrex-plc---Interim-Results-2023.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-06-14",
   "doc": "OPS",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -3,
   "q": "With no step up in demand going into the final quarter currently visible, and the resulting lower industrial revenue expectations, our full year adjusted PBT is now expected to be between £80m-£85m.",
   "file": "20230614_VCT_Trading-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-07-06",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "Overall, our Outlook is unchanged from what we recently communicated, with full-year adjusted (pre-exceptional) PBT expected to be in the range of £80m-£85m.",
   "file": "20230706_VCT_Victrex-plc---Q3-Interim-Management-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-12-05",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "The Group is expecting good progress in revenue and PBT for FY 2024, subject to an improving macro-economic outlook.",
   "file": "20231205_VCT_Victrex-plc---Preliminary-Results-2023.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-02-09",
   "doc": "Q1 TU",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -3,
   "q": "However, a continuation of the current macro-economic conditions makes achieving a profit growth outcome for the year more challenging and requires a further step up in run rates for the remainder of FY 2024.",
   "file": "20240209_VCT_AGM-&-Q1-Interim-Management-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-05-13",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "However, as previously communicated, we are not expecting PBT progress for the year as a whole.",
   "file": "20240513_VCT_Victrex-plc---Interim-Results-2024.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-07-04",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "Unless Medical improves above current run-rates, the opportunity to deliver a slightly better PBT performance in H2 2024, versus H2 2023 - in line with our previous guidance - will be challenging.",
   "file": "20240704_VCT_Q3-Interim-Management-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-12-03",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY25",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "In summary, we have the opportunity to deliver underlying PBT growth ahead of volume growth, after the impact of currency, which is now a £7m-£8m headwind to PBT in FY 2025.",
   "file": "20241203_VCT_Victrex-plc---Preliminary-Results-2024.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2025-02-07",
   "doc": "Q1 TU",
   "fy": "FY25",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "Based on our momentum at this early stage, our guidance remains for at least mid-single digit volume growth for FY 2025, with underlying PBT growth ahead of volume growth.",
   "file": "20250207_VCT_AGM-and-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2025-05-12",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY25",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "For H2, our target is to deliver PBT similar to H2 2024, driving some PBT growth in constant currency on a full year basis.",
   "file": "20250512_VCT_Victrex-plc-–-Interim-Results-2025.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2025-07-08",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY25",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "Whilst we are targeting H2 underlying PBT to be slightly improved on H1 underlying PBT of £23.2m, a continuation of Q3 sales mix and ASP trends for the remainder of the year, particularly in Medical Spine, would result in H2 underlying PBT being at a broadly similar level as H1.",
   "file": "20250708_VCT_Q3-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2025-12-02",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY26",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "Mindful of wider macro-economic conditions: targeting solid progress on FY 2025; H2 weighting reflects normal seasonality and the higher FX headwind in H1 2026",
   "file": "20251202_VCT_Preliminary-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2026-02-06",
   "doc": "Q1 TU",
   "fy": "FY26",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "Whilst we continue to be mindful of wider macroeconomic conditions, our full year guidance remains unchanged. As previously communicated, performance will be weighted to the second half.",
